Consider the given two statements:
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><b>Assertion (A):</b></span></td><td>Pollen grain exine has prominent apertures called germ pores where sporopollenin is absent.</td></tr><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><b>Reason (R):</b></span></td><td>Germ pore is the structure through which the germ tube or pollen tube makes its exit on germination.</td></tr></tbody></table>
&nbsp;

<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td><b>(A)</b> is True but <b>(R)</b> is False</td></tr><tr><td>2.</td><td>Both <b>(A)</b> and <b>(R)</b> are True and <b>(R)</b> does not explain <b>(A)</b></td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td>Both <b>(A)</b> and <b>(R)</b> are True and <b>(R)</b> explains <b>(A)</b></td></tr><tr><td>4.</td><td><b>(A)</b> is False but <b>(R)</b> is True</td></tr></tbody></table>
